                                "sense_id": "6a917e7b-e893-373c-9d0e-970b567120be",
                                "text": "Abravanel, for example, chooses to argue at length in favor of gilgulim in his commentary on the section of the Torah that discusses yibbum."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "76ca0bf0-1426-49ba-a96e-e845cfd59d3c",
                                "sense_id": "6a917e7b-e893-373c-9d0e-970b567120be",
                                "text": "The limitation of gilgul to men here is intriguing. Gilgul, among other things, is a process of purification from the sins of past lives, an alternative to the more anguished purification of Gehenna."
                            }
                        ]
